**Plan: JSON reads `buildRows()` straight, the table stays untouched.**

One call to make first. The table drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose, per the note in [format.js:3](src/format.js:3). I read "same data" as the full row from `buildRows()`, not the 4 table columns. Say the word if you meant column parity.

```js
// cli.js
const args = argv.slice(1);
const json = args.includes('--json');
if (args.some((a) => a !== '--json')) { /* usage, return 1 */ }
process.stdout.write(json ? JSON.stringify(buildRows(), null, 2) : toTable(buildRows()));
```

Sort order holds either way. `USAGE` gains `[--json]`.
